  "description": "Which shift an instant belongs to (ADR-0024, ADR-0034 §2), hand-written: the shift running at that instant, else the one starting within 60 minutes after it, else none. Shifts are wall-clock times on the site's clock; an end not after the start ends the next day, equal times mean 24 hours; no shift starts on a non-working day. A start or end inside a spring-forward gap moves forward by the gap; one inside a fall-back overlap takes the earlier offset; a shift the clock change makes empty does not happen. Read by ShiftCalendarVectorsTests (server, NodaTime) and shifts.test.ts (field app, Intl), so the tablet preselects the shift the server will store (P2.5, TC-P2-FO-001). Times: 'at', 'startsAt', 'endsAt' are UTC instants; 'date' is the site's local date the shift starts on.",
